<title>USA: Zilog debuts keyboard, shares rise.</title>
<headline>Zilog debuts keyboard, shares rise.</headline>
<dateline>CAMPBELL, Calif. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zilog Inc said it debuted a new keyboard controller family, the Z86KXX series.</p>
<p>It said the family exceeds industry-standard requirements and does not need costly external components and is aimed at the traditional PC market and the emerging wireless Internet market. The series has improved Electrostatic Discharge (ESD) and Electrical Fast Transient (EFT) performance, and cuts Electromagnetic Interference (EMI).</p>
<p>Shares of Zilog rose 1-3/8, or almost seven percent, to 21-1/4 on the New York Stock Exchange in late morning trading.</p>
